  "notes": "The main event, Tommy Grady against Brett Wayne, closes with no announced result: the referee is distracted, Wayne lifts the \"Ultimate Brawlers Trophy\", and one commentator protests that Wayne was beaten and asks whether he is \"our first Ultimate Brawlers Trophy holder?!\" while the other cheers him; the text declares no winner, so the row carries none. The fed's own news of 21 December 2002 bills the match \"for the FBA Trophy\" (\"the UBC Future Brawler Trophy Award\"), and its post-show news says only \"THE trophy was awarded!\", naming no winner: a trophy, not one of the four belts. No belt is put on the line in any match on the three shows, and the fed's own Champions page (captured 14 February 2003) still reads \"[none]\" for all four of its titles."
 }
